en cast in  xxx4 when the fast and furious franchise  began  in 2001 jaw rule was one of the biggest  rappers in the world  he was in the process of making the  transition to acting and appeared in a  very small role in the fast and the  furious as  a character named edwin who went up  against paul walker and ven diesel's  characters in a street race  he did not win  interestingly ja rule could have gone on  to be one of the faces of the franchise  if he'd been  interested in an interview with grant  land john singleton the director of too  fast  too furious recalled jaw got too big for  himself he turned it down he turned down  a half a million dollars to be in the  sequel singleton said he repeatedly  tried to get jaw rolled to the table but  eventually decided to swap his character  out for one played by a different rapper  ludacris who has since appeared in more  than half of the fast and furious films  apparently ludacris wasn't the first  potential replacement for jaw rule  originally rapper redman was eyed to  take on the role  once jaw rule dropped out of too fast  too furious redman was apparently geared  up to replace him he apparently had to  drop out due to scheduling conflicts the  tv series method and red came out around  the same time  as did a few other projects instead the  role went to ludicrous  just like ja rule redman's acting career  has been fairly stagnant  since this role passed him by it would  have been interesting to see how the  franchise might have evolved if either  one of them had been cast instead of  ludicrous  even though the fast and furious  franchise has become a blockbuster  series over the years it took a few  films for it to find its footing and  figure out what it wanted to be  most of the main players have stuck with  it over the long haul but the core group  didn't come together overnight  in fact in 2017 a producer revealed that  timothy oliphant  was initially targeted to star in the  first film apparently when the fast 